/**
 * Wave 4, family 5 (24 Sept 2026): the lymphoma and leukaemia entities the WHO Classification of Haematolymphoid
 * Tumours (5th edition, WHO-HAEM5, 2022) names and the corpus had only as strings or public-list names
 * (docs/CANCER-PAGES.md). Under marginal zone lymphoma: extranodal (MALT), splenic, nodal and primary cutaneous marginal
 * zone lymphoma. Under follicular lymphoma: primary cutaneous follicle centre lymphoma. Under cutaneous T-cell lymphoma:
 * Sezary syndrome. Under peripheral T-cell lymphoma: nodal TFH lymphoma of angioimmunoblastic type and hepatosplenic
 * T-cell lymphoma. Under diffuse large B-cell lymphoma: intravascular large B-cell lymphoma. Under non-Hodgkin lymphoma:
 * lymphomatoid granulomatosis. Under leukaemia: T-cell prolymphocytic leukaemia, T-cell large granular lymphocytic
 * leukaemia, splenic B-cell lymphoma/leukaemia with prominent nucleoli (the WHO-HAEM5 home of B-cell prolymphocytic
 * leukaemia) and mixed-phenotype acute leukaemia. Under paediatric AML: myeloid leukaemia of Down syndrome. Under
 * Burkitt lymphoma: Burkitt leukaemia.
 *
 * Rule cases: B-cell prolymphocytic leukaemia was discontinued as an entity by WHO-HAEM5 and is written under the new
 * name with B-PLL as an alias; "acute biphenotypic leukaemia" is the old name for mixed-phenotype acute leukaemia and is
 * an alias; "acute eosinophilic leukaemia" and "acute myeloid dendritic cell leukaemia" from the public list are not
 * entities in WHO-HAEM5 (eosinophilia is a feature of the myeloid/lymphoid neoplasms with tyrosine kinase fusions, and
 * the dendritic cell leukaemia is blastic plasmacytoid dendritic cell neoplasm, which has its own page), so neither
 * gets a page; "precursor B lymphoblastic leukaemia" is B-ALL, covered by the acute lymphoblastic leukaemia page and its
 * risk-group subpages; "orbital lymphoma" is a site, mostly ocular adnexal MALT lymphoma, and is a string on that page;
 * "primary cutaneous immunocytoma" is the old name of primary cutaneous marginal zone lymphoma; chronic myelomonocytic
 * leukaemia already had a page. Every figure is quoted from the paper or page named beside it. Registered in
 * src/data/index.ts as cancersWave4Haematology.
 */
